\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({csc}^{3}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta +9{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta (1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186483506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1045 "Further Properties of Line Integrals of Scalar Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186483441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482801 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "495233f9-f743-506d-b5fc-eaec14701f70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186482823 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{7\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16+10\\operatornam